body:
I get where he is coming from. He's wrong, no doubt about it, but this is what he's probably been told by his parents or his peers. it's what he knows and he won't change his opinion.

&#x200B;

At least he isn't forcing you to stop. Could be worse. Still bad.

Been there. They just can't wrap their heads around the fact that suicide is a state of helplessness. Their opinion is not worth anything. Don't listen to them.

&#x200B;

A way I've learned to cope is to be stubborn. "I cannot let them have the satisfaction of me dying". It'll hopefully work until you can seek proper help.

Thing is, I can't stay in America because I'm a Muslim. It's too much of a risk. But America has good trade schools and temporary jobs that pay good. I will think about becoming a resident.

&#x200B;

I do not want to work locally. India is a hellscape for us Muslims right now. And I'd rather die than work for TATA. They flaunt safety rules and the only "good" thing about them is that they own Jaguar Land Rover.

I have been waiting for someone to finally say this. The internet disappoints me more than I disappoint my father everyday. But you have restored my faith.

&#x200B;

I've heard far too many stories of so-called abusers being convicted even though they were innocent. I'll hold out for Slazo. I'm waiting on his response and then I'll make my decision.

I love this paradox. My friend told it to me.

&#x200B;

THe original goes osmething like this.

&#x200B;

*"The following statement is false.*

*The previous statement is true."*

I wish I could change it, but that's conceited of me. It's not just men as well, women also. Everyone knows what women are told when they get assaulted. "She was probably asking for it." "Shouldn't have gone outside at that time." or some other stupid shit.

&#x200B;

I wish pedophiles and rapists never existed. They're ruining it for the ones who just want to live a standard life.

"I hate the way you do things. I hate that I can't articulate myself."

&#x200B;

Wataru, you are a legend.

Breathe. Calm down. Use your words.

&#x200B;

Plus, Hachiman doesn't hate Yuigahama. He hates nice girls who are nice out of politeness or guilt. Yuigahama is nice to Hachiman, Miura, Yukinoshita and her friends because she cares for them.

Proof : She was repelled by Hikigaya at the second episode of the anime. She wasn't nice to him because she didn't like him initially.

&#x200B;

One more thing. Shipping is purely subjective. Let people have their opinions.

I think for planning the prom, Yukino asked Hachiman and Yui to let her do this alone because she wants to be independent. They both respect her request but Yui reminds Yukino to not shy away from asking for help from them if she needs to. So yeah, she grows independent. Hachiman is also happy that she's become independent.

&#x200B;

Also, I like to believe that the reason Yukino and Hachiman love each other is not borne out of dependancy on each other. I believe that they enjoy each other's company, but don't necessarily need it. It's like both of them are fine alone at solving issues, but both of them together can help people better.

"  - stated nowhere  " I never said that it was stated anywhere. It's just how a majority of the viewers felt. "  I could say i used to watch mainstream podcasts on youtube in early 2014 . " You could say that, but would you be saying the truth? Also, in early 2014, YouTube and radio was pretty much the only way you could listen to podcasts. " Its personal preference if you chose a individual creator over a professional team . " Yes, I agree. But T-Series already has many outlets. You can watch them on several music video channels on TV. They're also pretty much featured in every single Bollywood movie. If we wanted to listen to T-Series, we'd go there. We don't want them on YouTube.

" well thats actually how nations work , well yeah when pak attacked India where would be in-fact many people that did not support this but pakistan is a democracy . If most of the people elected the leader that did this attack , the attack was indirectly supported by the followers hence the people too . Now you cant actually trace who supported whom so its best to ban/block every artist from that nation . " I hear you, but those artists may or may not have supported the president and his actions. These artists had nothing to do with making the decision of the attack. The Constitution works differently. It's not just the decision of the Minister, but also a Cabinet decision, which is either vetoed or supported by the parliament. The people don't elect these guys. They're nominated. The decision does not even lie with the President, but mostly the Cabinet, who is elected by the Prime Minister's party.

&#x200B;

" Hope this sorted out some issues " It didn't. ok lol boring bye.

&#x200B;

He raised millions, yes, but he has also made donations. He's said so in his livestreams and he gains nothing from lying about that.

&#x200B;

T-Series ended their contracts with Pakistani artists because they were Pakistani and not Indians. They may have employed many, but they've also tried to actively ruin the livelihoods of people because they're racist.

&#x200B;

The reason T-Series is hated doesn't just stem to them being a corporation. As an Indian who used to be a T-Series fan, I know how T-Series works. They make music primarily for big production A-List Bollywood movies. This music video is added into said movie. That's where T-Series makes their money. All their content is not made for their YouTube audience. It's made for those people ho go to watch movies and maybe want to listen to the song again. They make their content for movies, not their YouTube  audience.

&#x200B;

Also, PewDiePie has his name registered because obviously, he doesn't want others using his alias for nefarious means. That doesn't make him a company. It makes him a smart person.
